e exists. manifest.json lists the EHR MCP server, native tool names and one peer, but not registries, identity services (token exchange, chat JWKS), gateways (egress proxy), stop channels (control table), audit services (Firehose), or the model provider.\"\n$A check E01.2 --met no --evidence release/manifest.json:43 --quote '\"owner\": \"ehr-integrations@northbay-clinics.example\"' --note \"Each manifest entry has a single owner. None names both an agent-team owner and a platform or vendor owner.\"\n$A check E01.3 --met no --evidence src/config.ts:62 --quote 'tokenExchangeUrl: process.env.TOKEN_EXCHANGE_URL ?? \"https://sts.northbay-clinics.example/oauth2/token\",' --note \"Called services absent from manifest.json: STS token exchange, chat JWKS (config.ts:58), payments API (payments.ts:9), SMS API (sms.ts:8), Anthropic API, Secrets Manager, DynamoDB, Firehose, JWKS from attestation jku (eligibility-a2a.ts:83).\"\n$A check E02.1 --met no --evidence Dockerfile:4 --quote \"COPY package.json package-lock.json ./\" --note \"package.json pins direct deps exactly, but no package-lock.json exists in the repo, so transitive packages float. The remote EHR MCP server is pinned only by TLS cert (manifest.json:42), not by version.\"\n$A check E02.2 --met no --evidence .github/workflows/ci.yml:20 --quote \"- run: npm ci --ignore-scripts\" --note \"The deploy workflow verifies the app image with cosign (deploy.yml:66). No npm audit signatures or sigstore check runs for packages, and the distroless base image (Dockerfile:10) is digest-pinned but its publisher signature is not verified.\"\n$A check E02.3 --met no --evidence .github/workflows/ci.yml:22 --quote \"- run: npm test\" --note \"No vulnerability scan (npm audit, osv-scanner, trivy, grype) in ci.yml or deploy.yml. ECR scan_on_push (main.tf:92) scans the image after push and does not gate a release.\"\n$A check E02.4 --met no --evidence package.json:16 --quote '\"dependencies\": {' --note \"No dependency approval records name publisher, permissions or update source for packages, the EHR MCP server, or the payments and SMS services. No recorded exception for remote services.\"\n$A check E03.1 --met no --evidence src/tools/registry.ts:126 --quote \"for (const t of scan.acceptedTools) {\" --note \"Discovered EHR tools are registered as soon as the scan passes. No owner approval of a versioned definition, no stored description/schema hash. The allowlist (tools.allowlist.yaml) is by name only, and registry.definitions() (loop.ts:50) shows every registered tool to the model.\"\n$A check E03.2 --met no --evidence src/server.ts:48 --quote \"const { reportedName, meta } = await ehr.catalog();\" --note \"Catalog is loaded once at startup. No fingerprint is computed or compared on any path, and no notifications/tools/list_changed handler exists. Sessions are re-created every 4 minutes (ehr-mcp.ts:66) without re-listing tools.\"\n$A check E03.3 --met no --evidence src/tools/registry.ts:131 --quote 'definition: toDefinition(`${serverId}__${t.name}`, t),' --note \"There is no fingerprint mismatch branch. Whatever definition the server reports at load is used.\"\n$A check E03.4 --met unknown --evidence release/manifest.json:41 --quote '\"url\": \"https://ehr-mcp.internal.northbay-clinics.example/mcp\",' --note \"EHR MCP server is remote; manifest records URL and TLS cert pin (manifest.json:42) but no implementation version, attestation, remote visibility limits, or review date. Implementation not visible from this repo.\"\n$A check E03.6 --met no --evidence src/config.ts:44 --quote 'export const policy = loadYaml<Policy>(\"config/policy.yaml\");' --note \"Policy is read once at start from files baked into the image. executor.ts:47 records policyVersion in audit, but there is no tool quarantine, propagation bound, or rollback guard against restoring revoked grants. kill-switch.ts halts runs and tenants, not individual tools.\"\n$A flag E03 --evidence src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:78 --note \"c.listTools() result goes straight to registration with no fingerprint compare (prescan H011)\"\n$A prescan H011 --verdict confirmed --item E03 --reason \"listTools output is registered without any approved fingerprint compare; see registry.ts:126 and server.ts:48\"\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6047,"cache_read_input_tokens":78607,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6047},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b66f2e4-48ab-4c3d-8d4a-2cb61810e167","uuid":"5eca66c0-d828-485c-a837-8d191bfbc467","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:07:37.386Z","request_id":"req_011CgDcq5XQqnkn7D9iSFZss","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Mb8v9j53Ck8gEHCWfxP1YV":{"command":"cd /private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-batch-afblo_q9/skill && P=/Users/brenn/.cache/uv/builds-v0/.tmpR1cD4H/bin/python; F=../agent/brace-findings.json; A=\"$P scripts/answer.py $F\"\n$A check C08.1 --met no --evidence src/server.ts:36 --quote \"setAgentTypeId(typeId);\" --note \"Records carry the computed type id, but a mismatch with manifest.agentTypeId (server.ts:32-35) only logs and a metric; the process keeps running and stamps a value that resolves to no stored manifest. reminders.ts:13 never compares at all. No store keyed by agent type id exists in the repo; the manifest is one file baked into the image (Dockerfile:19).\"\n$A check C08.2 --met no --evidence src/agent/classifier.ts:45 --quote \"res = await client.messages.create(\" --note \"The intent classifier is a model call that routes the run to staff or agent. Its audit record (loop.ts:42 intent.classified) carries no context size. Only the agent loop's model.decision (loop.ts:66) records context. SDK retry (loop.ts:15 m